{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"Under [Rule 2a-5(b), (e)(4)](https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/17/270.2a-5), the board may designate **the ETF’s investment adviser, but not a sub-adviser**, to perform fair-value determinations, subject to board oversight.\n\nThe designee must provide **written board reporting**:\n\n- **At least quarterly:** Board-requested reports/materials and a summary or description of material fair-value matters, including material changes in valuation risks/conflicts, methodologies or deviations, and pricing-service selection/oversight.\n- **At least annually:** An assessment of the valuation process’s adequacy and effectiveness, including methodology-testing results and the adequacy of allocated resources.\n- **Promptly:** Notice of matters materially affecting designated investments’ fair values, including significant deficiencies/material weaknesses in the valuation process or material NAV-calculation errors. Notice must meet the board’s deadline, **never later than five business days after awareness**, with timely follow-up as the board determines.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Designation does not eliminate the board’s oversight responsibility."}}
